    description: "WHAT\nTypeScript / JavaScript callables that emit no symbol, or whose parameters are in no hash (seen while building PR #2370's parameter-mark fix):\n1. A class field with an arrow-function value (m = (x?: number) => x) is a field whose id hashes only its type annotation: its parameters are in no id.\n2. An object-literal value (key: function () {} / key: () => {}) and export default function (...) {} emit no symbol. A callback declared inside one still hashes the holder's signature in its scope label (5 such ids moved in the 51-tree comparison: workadventure Stores/ErrorStore.ts line 27, a callback inside addErrorMessage: (e, options?: {...}) => {...}).\n\nREPRO\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v20_11242026/ts/RESULTS.md, residuals 2 and 3; bump/mine2_run1.txt (\"ts UNEXPLAINED\").\n\nNOT CHECKED\nWhether emitting these is wanted (it adds symbols and, for 1, changes hashed input: a scheme bump, owner-ruled). Related open items: WI-dokos (TypeScript/JavaScript same-named locals of unnamed holders).\n\nFound 2026-11-24 while building PR #2370 (stable-id v20). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v20_11242026/STATUS.md and the package RESULTS.md named above."  # 907b
